# GitHub parses this file directly and cannot read Jekyll data, so the title and
# author values here are maintained separately from _config.yml. Change both together.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: If you use this framework, please cite it.
title: "Reading Regulatory Order: A Five-Layer Procedure"
abstract: >-
  A five-layer procedure for reading how regulatory order forms and reaches the
  firms standing under it, across AI-related value chains: semiconductors,
  computing, cloud, data centers. Layer A reads conditions and Layer B reads events as two
  independent classification axes; Layer C is downstream of both, describing
  how they leave a trace in the record; Layer D and Layer E describe
  distribution and re-formation once an order exists.
type: software
authors:
